From 50b9b41b3da6852f26d9472a0dcf587d4c7fbf51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Junod <donujp@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:06:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reader: bound Exp-Golomb codes and preserve integer precision

Both reader backends shifted by the untrusted unary prefix length and
decoded signed magnitudes through f64. A 64-zero prefix could panic and
large signed values lost precision. Share private checked integer
decoding, preserve the full u64 and i64 endpoints, and stop prefix
scanning after 65 zero bits. Public reader APIs and writer arithmetic
remain unchanged.

Default, all-feature and bitstream-only reader suites pass. Backend
regressions cover endpoints, numeric overflow, truncated payloads,
cursor preservation and a prefix with no marker.
